{"format":1,"seq":531,"writes":[{"type":"entry","value":{"model":[{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm thinking through a nested-run guard for pi-action: setting an environment variable like PI_ACTION_RUN that index.ts checks at startup to detect and block recursive invocations, erroring out early if already set. I'm also considering whether push.ts needs the same guard, since a nested push from the agent is fast-forward only and less risky, but applying it anyway for consistency.\n\nSeparately, I'm tracing the \"has settled\" crash to pit's onShellProgress handler firing after settlement in a socket data callback, causing an uncaught throw — the fix belongs in pit itself, so I'm checking whether I can even open a PR there given the app token's likely repo-scoped permissions.\n\nFor now I'll start on follow-up 1: switching off the feat branch to main and creating a new fix branch for the nested-run guard, since there's no issue number to reference. Then I'll dig into the pit repository to confirm reachability before attempting anything there.\n\n","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"Two follow-ups: a nested-run guard (in this repo) and the `has settled` crash (in pit or pi-durable). First I'll find where pit and pi-durable live and whether this token can open PRs there."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_bdrk_01CeEkkDmLZYg4muj9JWDgWs","name":"typescript","arguments":{"code":"// @pit: {\"label\": \"Find pit and pi-durable upstream repos and access\"}\nasync ({ shell: { exec } }) => {\n  const r = await exec(`grep -n \"pit\" .github/workflows/pi-assistant.yml | head; npm view pit name version repository.url 2>&1 | head; npm view @earendil-works/pi-durable repository.url 2>&1 | head -3; grep -o '\"repository\"[^}]*}' node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-durable/package.json; gh api user --jq .login 2>&1; gh api repos/cv/pi-action --jq .permissions 2>&1`, { timeoutMs: 60000 });\n  return r.stdout + r.stderr;\n}"}}],"api":"anthropic-messa